<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Transylvanian Saxons</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Transylvanian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxons</a> are a German-speaking people settled in southern and north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a> from the mid-twelfth century, first under King Géza II. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diploma-andreanum">Andreanum</a> of 1224 granted them collective self-government, and their towns, such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sibiu">Hermannstadt</a> (Sibiu) and Kronstadt (Brașov), and their fortified churches flourished. Most emigrated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> and the fall of communism in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/transylvanian-saxons.jpg" alt="Transylvanian Saxons" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Argean · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Transylvania_Saxons.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
